{"units": [{"id": "ma-orth1", "translation": "by (in oaths)"}, {"id": "ma-def1", "translation": "by (in oaths)"}, {"id": "ma-quote1", "translation": "by the perfect Justice of my child"}, {"id": "ma_mater-orth1", "translation": "mother"}, {"id": "ma_mater-def1", "translation": "mother"}, {"id": "ma_mater-note1", "translation": "It is read in Theocritus 15, 89: μᾶ, πόθεν ὤνθρωπος [mother, where are you from, man?]. Similar examples of apocope are πᾶ [pa] and βᾶ [ba] for πατήρ [father] and βασιλεύς [king], which we discussed under βᾶ."}, {"id": "ma_mater-quote1", "translation": "Mother Earth, mother Earth"}, {"id": "ma_mater-word1", "translation": "mother, where are you from, man?"}, {"id": "ma_mater-word2", "translation": "pa (for father)"}, {"id": "ma_mater-word3", "translation": "ba (for king)"}, {"id": "ma_mater-word4", "translation": "father"}, {"id": "ma_mater-word5", "translation": "king"}, {"id": "ma_mater-word6", "translation": "ba"}, {"id": "magnetikos-orth1", "translation": "Magnetic"}, {"id": "magnetikos-def1", "translation": "Magnetic"}, {"id": "magnetikos-quote1", "translation": "Magnetic earth"}, {"id": "magos-orth1", "translation": "Magus"}, {"id": "magos-def1", "translation": "Magus"}, {"id": "magos-note1", "translation": "That the Magi are a people around Media is established from Herodotus and elsewhere: see Thes. vol. 5 p. 489. But since this name is pronounced with a short first syllable, it cannot be written Μᾶγος [Magus] with Turnebus, but it is more probable that Aeschylus said ῎Αραβος [Arabus] with the middle syllable lengthened, a liberty which could more easily be excused in a barbarian, unknown name than in the very well-known name Μάγος [Magus], whose constant measure is this, not Μᾶγος [Magus]."}, {"id": "magos-quote1", "translation": "and Magus, Arabus, and Artames the Bactrian, where the scholiast noted: Magus is an ethnic, Arabus a proper name."}, {"id": "magos-word1", "translation": "Magi"}, {"id": "magos-word2", "translation": "Magus (with long alpha)"}, {"id": "magos-word3", "translation": "Arabus"}, {"id": "magos-word4", "translation": "Magus"}, {"id": "magos-word5", "translation": "Magus (with long alpha)"}, {"id": "maza-orth1", "translation": "barley-cake, bread"}, {"id": "maza-def1", "translation": "barley-cake, bread"}, {"id": "maza-quote1", "translation": "having been sold, to endure to get a slave's barley-cake. Thus Engerus corrected for μάζης βία [force of barley-cake]. Deceived by this corruption, Triclinius interpolated: having been sold, to endure and to touch the yoke by force."}, {"id": "mazos-orth1", "translation": "breast"}, {"id": "mazos-note1", "translation": "See μαστός."}, {"id": "mazos-word1", "translation": "breast"}, {"id": "mathos-orth1", "translation": "learning, knowledge, wisdom"}, {"id": "mathos-def1", "translation": "learning, knowledge, wisdom"}, {"id": "mathos-quote1", "translation": "who has established that learning comes by suffering, to hold it as valid. Here πάθος [suffering] and μάθος [learning] are paired, as elsewhere πάθημα [suffering] and μάθημα [lesson] are often paired."}, {"id": "maia-orth1", "translation": "mother"}, {"id": "maia-def1", "translation": "mother"}, {"id": "maia-quote1", "translation": "O mother Earth. See Thes. vol. 5 p. 501."}, {"id": "maia_proper-orth1", "translation": "Maia"}, {"id": "maia_proper-def1", "translation": "Maia, mother of Mercury"}, {"id": "maia_proper-quote1", "translation": "the son of Maia"}, {"id": "maia_proper-quote2", "translation": "Hermes, son of Maia and Zeus"}, {"id": "maia_proper-word1", "translation": "Maia"}, {"id": "maimao-orth1", "translation": "to rage, to be eager"}, {"id": "maimao-def1", "translation": "to rage, to be eager"}, {"id": "maimao-quote1", "translation": "nearby rages a two-footed serpent"}, {"id": "mainas-orth1", "translation": "Maenad, Bacchant"}, {"id": "mainas-def1", "translation": "Fury"}, {"id": "mainas-def2", "translation": "Bacchant"}, {"id": "mainas-quote1", "translation": "the wrath of the Maenads who watch mortals"}, {"id": "mainas-quote2", "translation": "father Theoinus, yoker of the Maenads"}, {"id": "mainolis-orth1", "translation": "frenzied, mad"}, {"id": "mainolis-def1", "translation": "frenzied, mad"}, {"id": "mainolis-quote1", "translation": "frenzied mind"}, {"id": "mainomai-orth1", "translation": "to rage, to be mad"}, {"id": "mainomai-def1", "translation": "to rage, to be mad"}, {"id": "mainomai-def2", "translation": "middle form of the perfect"}, {"id": "mainomai-quote1", "translation": "raging Ares breathes upon"}, {"id": "mainomai-quote2", "translation": "with frenzied mind"}, {"id": "mainomai-quote3", "translation": "with maddened heart"}, {"id": "mainomai-quote4", "translation": "with maddened strife"}, {"id": "mainomai-quote5", "translation": "the mind rages with laments"}, {"id": "mainomai-quote6", "translation": "who is indeed mad"}, {"id": "mainomai-quote7", "translation": "maddened by dishonorable toils"}, {"id": "mainomai-quote8", "translation": "I hear that you are mad with no small disease"}, {"id": "maiomai-orth1", "translation": "to seek, to desire"}, {"id": "maiomai-def1", "translation": "to seek, to desire"}, {"id": "maiomai-note1", "translation": "μαιομένοις [seeking] seems certain, but the emendation of the rest is uncertain."}, {"id": "maiomai-quote1", "translation": "but for me to obtain the blessings of moderation, to see them well for those who seek"}, {"id": "maiomai-quote2", "translation": "to see moderation for those who seek"}, {"id": "maiomai-word1", "translation": "seeking"}, {"id": "maiotikos-orth1", "translation": "Maeotic"}, {"id": "maiotikos-def1", "translation": "Maeotic"}, {"id": "maiotikos-note1", "translation": "Adjective derived from Μαιώται [Maeotae], which is the name of a Scythian people, about which see Thes. vol. 5 p. 510."}, {"id": "maiotikos-quote1", "translation": "to cross the Maeotic strait"}, {"id": "maiotikos-word1", "translation": "Maeotae"}, {"id": "maiotis-orth1", "translation": "Maeotis"}, {"id": "maiotis-def1", "translation": "Maeotis"}, {"id": "maiotis-quote1", "translation": "around the Maeotic lake"}, {"id": "makar-orth1", "translation": "blessed, divine"}, {"id": "makar-def1", "translation": "blessed, divine"}, {"id": "makar-def2", "translation": "feminine μάκαιρα"}, {"id": "makar-note1", "translation": "μάκαρες [blessed ones] very often refers to the gods, either with θεοί [gods] added or omitted."}, {"id": "makar-quote1", "translation": "the young commander of the blessed ones"}, {"id": "makar-quote2", "translation": "the ruler of the blessed ones"}, {"id": "makar-quote3", "translation": "O blessed ones, well-seated"}, {"id": "makar-quote4", "translation": "by the prayers of the blessed ones"}, {"id": "makar-quote5", "translation": "for after the blessed ones and the might of Zeus"}, {"id": "makar-quote6", "translation": "to this man the blessed ones granted to take the city of Priam"}, {"id": "makar-quote7", "translation": "blessed ones of the underworld"}, {"id": "makar-quote8", "translation": "lord of lords, most blessed of the blessed"}, {"id": "makar-quote9", "translation": "blessed gods"}, {"id": "makar-quote10", "translation": "blessed queen Onca"}, {"id": "makar-word1", "translation": "blessed ones"}, {"id": "makar-word2", "translation": "gods"}, {"id": "makar-word3", "translation": "blessed (feminine)"}, {"id": "makarites-orth1", "translation": "blessed, deceased"}]}